    proposition: "The sans-ovation characterisation is documented in the distribution analytics with forensic precision. 378,571 downloads. Zero institutional backing. Zero mainstream media coverage. Zero advocacy organisation support. Zero legal aid. Zero NGO involvement. Zero promotional budget. The archive propagated to 378,571 people through none of the amplification mechanisms that institutional actors control — no mainstream media, no legal aid societies, no academic institutions, no NGOs, no advocacy organisations. The feat-in-obscurity is the terror they dread: not the 378,571 downloads (which they can attempt to contextualise or minimise), but the mechanism by which 378,571 downloads occurred without using any of their controlled channels. If the archive can reach 378,571 people without media, without legal aid, without NGOs, without academic institutions — then those channels are not the gatekeepers of public information that the institutional framework assumed they were. The terror is not the archive. The terror is the proof that the gatekeeping model no longer works.",
